\input docstrip

\keepsilent
\askforoverwritefalse

\declarepreamble\stylepreamble

This is the `ufrj-ic' unit style of the `ufrj' document class -- the data
and texts of the Instituto de Computacao (IC) of the Federal University of
Rio de Janeiro, for the dissertations and theses of its Programa de
Pos-Graduacao em Informatica (PPGI). It is generated from ufrj-ic.dtx by
docstrip; edit the .dtx source, not this file.

Copyright (C) 2008-2026 Vicente Helano F. Batista, George O. Ainsworth Jr.,
Geraldo Xexéo and Eduardo Mangeli.

This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
it under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 3 as
published by the Free Software Foundation.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the
GNU General Public License version 3 for more details.

You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
version 3 along with this package (see the COPYING.txt file).
If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.

\endpreamble

\declarepreamble\examplepreamble

This is a sample dissertation or thesis which illustrates the use of the `ufrj'
document class with the `ufrj-ic' unit style. It is generated from
ufrj-ic.dtx by docstrip.

Copyright (C) 2008-2026 Vicente Helano F. Batista, George O. Ainsworth Jr.,
Geraldo Xexéo and Eduardo Mangeli. Released under the GNU General Public
License version 3 (see the COPYING.txt file).

\endpreamble

\postamble
% end of `ufrj-ic' customized files
\endpostamble

\usedir{tex/latex/ufrj}
\generate{%
  \usepreamble\stylepreamble
  \file{ufrj-ic.sty}{\from{ufrj-ic.dtx}{package}}%
  \usepreamble\examplepreamble
  \file{ic-min-exemplo.tex}{\from{ufrj-ic.dtx}{icminexemplo}}%
  \file{ic-max-exemplo.tex}{\from{ufrj-ic.dtx}{icmaxexemplo}}%
}
\endbatchfile
